# clangd config for libhtttp — teaches the language server where htttp.h lives.
# The header sits in include/, not beside the .c files, so without a hint clangd
# floods every source/test with bogus "file not found" errors on #include
# "htttp.h". The Makefile passes -Iinclude, but clangd has no compile_commands
# database here, so it runs a generic fallback whose working directory is the
# *source file's own directory* (src/ or tests/). A plain -Iinclude would then
# resolve to src/include (nonexistent); -I../include resolves to lib/libhtttp/
# include for every .c under src/ and tests/ (all exactly one level deep). Build
# flags are unchanged; this only affects the editor.
CompileFlags:
  Add:
    - -I../include
